Direct scanout at a fractional output scale

Problem: direct scanout never happens on an output with a fractional scale (DP-3
at 1.5). The scanout check compares the surface's integer buffer scale with the
output scale, which can never be equal at 1.5. Every fullscreen game is then
composited. Present since Wayfire 0.9.0.
Fix (the maintainer's variant): no scale check; the buffer must have the
output's pixel size and transform and no viewport crop. A buffer of another
size is composited as before.
Upstream: https://github.com/WayfireWM/wayfire/issues/3253 (open). The maintainer
asked for this variant on 2026-11-22. PR and reply drafts:
~/Documents/Wayfire direct scanout/; not posted yet.
Remove when: the fix is on main. Check: a fullscreen game at scale 1.5 is
scanned out directly (no composition).
Base: wayfire 669bbe36.

